00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Our episodes deal with serious and often distressing incidents. If you feel at any time you need support, please contact your local crisis centre. For suggested phone numbers for confidential support, please see the show notes for this episode on your app or on our website. Today's episode involves crimes against children and won't be suitable for all listeners. Friday, April 13, 1973 was an exhausting day for the Kennedy family. 24-year-old Faye and her two young daughters, 5-year-old Stephanie and 17-month-old Deirdre, had just returned home to the small Queensland city of Ipswich after a six-week trip visiting
我们的剧集涉及严重且往往令人痛苦的事件。如果您在任何时候感到需要支持，请联系您当地的危机中心。如需获取保密支持的建议电话号码，请查看您应用中或我们网站上的本集节目说明。今天的剧集涉及针对儿童的犯罪，并不适合所有听众。1973年4月13日星期五，对肯尼迪一家来说是筋疲力尽的一天。24岁的费伊和她两个年幼的女儿，5岁的斯蒂芬妮和17个月大的迪尔德丽，刚刚结束了为期六周的探亲之旅，回到了昆士兰州伊普斯威奇市的小家。

2
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:36.000
relatives further up north. It had required a 17-hour bus ride home and none of them had gotten much sleep. Faye's husband Barry was recovering from knee surgery and the effort of hobbling around on crutches left him drained of energy. They took it slow that day. Stephanie and Deirdre were often excitable around bedtime, but as night approached they got ready for bed without protest. Faye prepared Deirdre's favourite meal, tomato soup with a side of asparagus spears.
这趟回家的旅程需要乘坐17个小时的巴士，她们都没怎么睡好。费伊的丈夫巴里正在从膝盖手术中恢复，拄着拐杖蹒跚而行的劳累让他精疲力竭。那天他们过得很慢。斯蒂芬妮和迪尔德丽在临近睡觉时通常很兴奋，但随着夜幕降临，她们没有抗拒就准备睡觉了。费伊准备了迪尔德丽最喜欢的饭菜：番茄汤配芦笋。

3
00:01:36.000 --> 00:02:12.000
After giving the girls a bath, Faye put Deirdre into a fresh nappy with a waterproof cover on top known as a pilcher. She then dressed her in a singlet and a new pair of pink pyjamas adorned with bunny motifs. Deirdre was excited about her new pyjamas and showed them off proudly to her father. The Kennedys lived in a two-bedroom single-story unit. Stephanie and Deirdre shared a small bedroom at the end of the hallway adjacent to their parents. The two girls were incredibly close.
给女孩们洗完澡后，费伊给迪尔德丽换上了一块干净的尿布，并在外面套上了一层防水罩，也就是所谓的“皮尔彻”。然后，她给迪尔德丽穿上一件背心和一套装饰着兔子图案的粉色新睡衣。迪尔德丽对她的新睡衣感到很兴奋，并自豪地向父亲展示。肯尼迪一家住在一套两居室的单层公寓里。斯蒂芬妮和迪尔德丽共用走廊尽头的一间小卧室，就在父母卧室的隔壁。这两个女孩关系非常亲密。

4
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:53.000
Stephanie doted on her baby sister whom she affectionately called a DD. At 7.30pm, Faye placed a sleepy Deirdre in her cot near the bedroom door. An hour later, she tucked Stephanie into her bed below the open window. Faye and Barry spent some time together before retiring to bed at around 10 o'clock. Faye checked in on her daughters one last time. Both girls were sleeping soundly. Faye pulled the aluminium sliding window and curtain shut before tenderly tucking the girls in and leaving the room.
斯蒂芬妮非常疼爱她的小妹妹，亲昵地称她为“DD”。晚上7点30分，费伊把昏昏欲睡的迪尔德丽放在卧室门口附近的婴儿床里。一小时后，她把斯蒂芬妮塞进窗户下方的床上。费伊和巴里在一起待了一会儿，然后在10点左右上床休息。费伊最后一次去看了看女儿们。两个女孩都睡得很香。费伊拉上铝制推拉窗和窗帘，然后温柔地为女孩们掖好被子，离开了房间。

5
00:02:53.000 --> 00:03:53.000
She fell asleep easily, worn out from the long day. The following morning, Faye was awoken suddenly by Stephanie shaking her shoulder. The five-year-old looked concerned. Wake up, she said. Deirdre's not in her bed. Faye Kennedy loved nothing more than being a mother. She cared for her two daughters full-time while Barry supported the family by working as an instrument fitter for the Royal Australian Air Force.
她很快就睡着了，因为漫长的一天让她疲惫不堪。第二天早上，费伊被斯蒂芬妮摇晃肩膀突然惊醒。这个五岁的孩子看起来很担心。她说：“醒醒，迪尔德丽不在她的床上。”费伊·肯尼迪最喜欢的就是做母亲。她全职照顾两个女儿，而巴里则在澳大利亚皇家空军担任仪表装配工，以此养家糊口。

6
00:03:53.000 --> 00:04:37.000
It was this role that had recently landed the Kennedys in Ipswich, located 40km west of Brisbane. Barry was transferred there in late 1972 and the family settled into the two-bedroom unit on Short Street. There's was one of four units in a small cream brick block owned by the Air Force. The move was just temporary while they awaited assignment of a bigger house. But the unit's location on the edge of town, just 350m from Limestone Park and a 15-minute drive from the Air Force base in the nearby suburb of Amberley, suited them fine for now.
正是这份工作让肯尼迪一家最近搬到了位于布里斯班以西40公里的伊普斯威奇。巴里于1972年底被调到那里，一家人搬进了肖特街的一套两居室公寓。这是空军拥有的一个小奶油色砖块建筑中的四套公寓之一。这次搬迁只是暂时的，他们还在等待分配更大的房子。但公寓位于城镇边缘，距离石灰岩公园仅350米，距离附近的安伯利郊区的空军基地仅15分钟车程，目前对他们来说很合适。

7
00:04:37.000 --> 00:05:11.000
The slow pace of Ipswich matched the Kennedys' small-town mentality. Having been raised in the outback, Barry and Faye were country kids at heart. Quiet and trusting, they had lived relatively sheltered lives and believed in the best of people. When the couple awoke to find baby Deirdre wasn't in her cot, they desperately searched their house. The 17-month-old had only recently started walking, having scooted around on her bottom until she'd managed to find her feet.
伊普斯威奇缓慢的节奏与肯尼迪一家的小镇心态相吻合。巴里和费伊在内陆地区长大，内心深处是乡村孩子。他们安静且容易信任他人，过着相对安稳的生活，并相信人性本善。当这对夫妇醒来发现婴儿迪尔德丽不在婴儿床里时，他们绝望地搜查了房子。这个17个月大的孩子最近才开始走路，之前一直是用屁股挪动，直到最近才学会站立。

8
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:49.000
She was still shaky on her legs and there was no way she could have climbed out of her cot or opened any doors on her own. Regardless, the Kennedys looked through the small unit, checking under beds and furniture as they called Deirdre's name. They searched outside before knocking on their neighbour's door. She hadn't seen Deirdre or heard anything out of the ordinary. The green open spaces offered by Limestone Park made it a popular recreation spot for residents of Ipswich.
她的腿还很虚弱，根本不可能自己爬出婴儿床或打开任何门。尽管如此，肯尼迪夫妇还是搜查了这间小公寓，检查了床下和家具下方，同时呼唤着迪尔德丽的名字。他们在外面搜寻了一番，然后敲响了邻居的门。邻居没有见过迪尔德丽，也没有听到任何异常情况。石灰岩公园提供的绿色开放空间使其成为伊普斯威奇居民的热门休闲场所。

9
00:05:49.000 --> 00:06:32.000
Located just a few minutes drive from the town centre, the sprawling park was framed by a blend of residential streets and main thoroughfares. And children alike frequented the area to exercise, play sports, and walk their pets among the mostly flatland dotted with a scattering of native trees. Ostrana Westy Mills was one such resident. The sun had barely risen on the morning of Saturday, April 14, 1973, as Westy trodded one of his horses across the Dewey Oval. There were few other people around, save for a jogger and a duo with a dog.
公园距离市中心仅几分钟车程，广阔的公园被住宅街道和主要干道环绕。孩子们经常在这里锻炼、玩耍和遛宠物，公园里大部分是平地，点缀着一些原生树木。奥斯特拉纳·韦斯蒂·米尔斯就是其中一位居民。1973年4月14日星期六的早晨，太阳刚刚升起，韦斯蒂牵着他的一匹马走过杜威椭圆形草坪。周围几乎没有其他人，除了一个慢跑者和一对带着狗的人。

10
00:06:32.000 --> 00:07:14.000
As Westy passed a public toilet block on the western edge of the park, he noticed something hanging off the edge of the flat tin roof. He pulled his horse to a stop so he could get a closer look. At first, Westy thought it was a ragdoll. He then realised what exactly he was looking at. Westy cried out in shock, help, there's a baby here. Westy Mills desperately climbed onto the toilet block roof and retrieved the baby's body. It was a young girl who had died a violent death.
当韦斯蒂经过公园西侧的一个公共厕所时，他注意到有什么东西挂在平坦的锡屋顶边缘。他勒住马停下来，以便看得更清楚。起初，韦斯蒂以为那是一个布娃娃。随后他意识到自己看到的究竟是什么。韦斯蒂惊恐地大喊：“救命，这里有个婴儿。”韦斯蒂·米尔斯拼命爬上厕所屋顶，取下了婴儿的尸体。那是一个死于暴力的小女孩。

11
00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:55.000
She was wearing a pink pajama top, but her pajama bottoms and nappy had been removed and tossed aside. In their place was women's underwear, a pair of blue panties, elastic step-ins with suspenders and a silk half-slip skirt. The local police were summoned along with detectives from Brisbane. The site made even the most seasoned investigators recoil. The baby's face and neck were covered in bruises and there was bruising to her lower thigh. There was a small abrasion near one of her eyes and on her upper lip.
她穿着一件粉色的睡衣上衣，但睡衣裤子和尿布已被脱掉并扔在一边。取而代之的是女性内衣：一条蓝色内裤、带有吊带的弹性紧身裤和一条丝绸半衬裙。当地警方被召集，布里斯班的侦探也随之赶到。现场让最老练的调查人员都感到反胃。婴儿的脸和脖子上布满了淤青，大腿下部也有淤青。她的一只眼睛附近和上唇上有一处小擦伤。

12
00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:33.000
She had been sexually assaulted and strangled. Around this time, a neighbour of the Kennedy family ran to the police station as neither of them had a phone. As soon as the officer on duty heard that a baby was missing from Short Street, he had no doubt. The baby in Limestone Park was Deirdre Kennedy. Ipswich's chief of police remarked, This, by its circumstances, is the most brutal murder I have ever seen.
她遭到了性侵犯和勒死。大约在这个时候，肯尼迪一家的一位邻居跑到了警察局，因为他们家里都没有电话。当值班警官听说肖特街有一个婴儿失踪时，他毫不怀疑。石灰岩公园里的婴儿就是迪尔德丽·肯尼迪。伊普斯威奇警察局长评论道：“从情况来看，这是我见过的最残忍的谋杀案。”

13
00:08:33.000 --> 00:09:07.000
Barry Kennedy was summoned to identify his daughter. He couldn't bring himself to tell Fay exactly what had happened, just that Deirdre had been killed. The devoted parents were beside themselves. They tried to hold it together for Stephanie's sake, but they were consumed by guilt as they blamed themselves for what had happened. Although Fay had checked the unit and closed the girl's window before she went to bed the night before, she hadn't locked the door.
巴里·肯尼迪被传唤去辨认他的女儿。他无法忍受告诉费伊到底发生了什么，只说迪尔德丽被杀了。这对深情的父母悲痛欲绝。他们试图为了斯蒂芬妮而坚强起来，但他们被内疚感所吞噬，因为他们责怪自己导致了这一切。尽管费伊在前一天晚上睡觉前检查了公寓并关上了女孩们的窗户，但她没有锁门。

14
00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:43.000
This wasn't unusual, Ipswich was considered a safe city and it was customary for residents to leave their doors unlocked. It wasn't in Fay or Barry's upbringing to be overly vigilant about securing their home. Police visited Short Street to look for evidence. Although Fay was certain she'd clicked the sliding window closed, it was now slightly ajar. Police dusted the property for unknown fingerprints. They'd already uncovered some on the door of the toilet block at Limestone Park.
这并不罕见，伊普斯威奇被认为是一个安全的城市，居民习惯于不锁门。费伊和巴里在成长过程中并没有养成过度警惕保护家园的习惯。警方走访了肖特街寻找证据。虽然费伊确信她已经关上了推拉窗，但现在窗户却微微敞开。警方对房产进行了指纹采集。他们已经在石灰岩公园的厕所门上发现了一些指纹。

15
00:09:43.000 --> 00:10:20.000
No foreign prints were detected on the Kennedy's window, but there was one on the front door. It couldn't be determined whether the killer had accessed the house via the door or the window. If they'd used the door, they would have had to skulk quietly down the short hallway at the risk of waking the parents. Had they used the window, they would have had to climb over Stephanie's bed. But the five-year-old hadn't stirred at any point, nor did she recall hearing or seeing anyone enter the room.
肯尼迪家的窗户上没有检测到外来指纹，但前门上有一个。无法确定凶手是通过门还是窗进入房子的。如果他们使用了门，他们必须悄悄地溜过短走廊，冒着惊醒父母的风险。如果他们使用了窗户，他们必须爬过斯蒂芬妮的床。但这个五岁的孩子在任何时候都没有被惊醒，她也不记得听到或看到任何人进入房间。

16
00:10:20.000 --> 00:11:04.000
Deirdre was painfully shy and her parents had no doubt that she would have cried if woken by a stranger. But no one in the Kennedy household had heard Deirdre crying. Although they couldn't rule out the possibility entirely, investigators didn't think that Deirdre had been strangled at the same time she was abducted. Either the killer had managed to scoop Deirdre up without waking her, or the rest of the family had been so exhausted from their long day that they'd slept through her tears. 73-year-old Cecil Carroll lived next door to the Kennedy's in a large, single-story
迪尔德丽非常害羞，她的父母毫不怀疑，如果被陌生人吵醒，她一定会哭。但肯尼迪家没有人听到迪尔德丽的哭声。虽然他们不能完全排除这种可能性，但调查人员认为迪尔德丽并不是在被绑架的同时被勒死的。要么是凶手在不惊醒她的情况下把迪尔德丽抱走了，要么是家里其他人因为漫长的一天太累了，以至于在她的哭声中睡着了。73岁的塞西尔·卡罗尔住在肯尼迪家隔壁的一栋大型单层房子里。

17
00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:40.000
house. The two properties were separated only by some overgrown shrubs. Cecil bordered there with the eight-member Borscht family and mostly kept to himself in his bedroom at the end of the house. On the night of Friday, April 13, Cecil hadn't been feeling well and was resting in bed. As he lit up a cigarette at around 10pm, he noticed something moving outside of his bedroom window. The window opened out to the home's wraparound veranda, which housed the makeshift washing
两处房产仅被一些杂草丛生的灌木隔开。塞西尔与八口之家的博尔什一家为邻，大部分时间都独自待在房子尽头的卧室里。1973年4月13日星期五晚上，塞西尔感觉不舒服，正在床上休息。晚上10点左右，当他点燃一支香烟时，他注意到卧室窗外有什么东西在动。窗户通向房子环绕式的阳台，那里设有临时的晾衣绳。

18
00:11:40.000 --> 00:12:22.000
line. At first, Cecil thought it was one of the Borscht kids, but as he watched on, he realized it was a male who looked to be aged between 18 and 20 years old. He was about 172cm tall, with a slender build of around 63kg. His hair was collar length and light brown to blonde in colour. After watching for a few minutes, Cecil realized the prowler was taking items from the washing line. He got out of bed and alerted the patriarch of the household, Arthur Borscht.
起初，塞西尔以为是博尔什家的孩子之一，但当他继续观察时，他意识到那是一个看起来在18到20岁之间的男性。他身高约172厘米，身材苗条，体重约63公斤。他的头发长及衣领，颜色从浅棕色到金色不等。观察了几分钟后，塞西尔意识到那个潜行者正在从晾衣绳上拿东西。他起床并通知了该户人家的家长亚瑟·博尔什。

19
00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:57.000
Arthur went outside and checked the veranda. There was no one there. He told Cecil to go back to bed. Shortly after, Arthur looked out the window and noticed the male figure walking towards the Air Force units next door. It was difficult to see anything through the darkness, but the figure appeared to be in his late teens and around 170cm tall. It was only upon closer inspection the following day that the Borschets realized several items
亚瑟走到外面检查了阳台。那里没有人。他告诉塞西尔回床上睡觉。不久之后，亚瑟向窗外望去，注意到那个男性身影正走向隔壁的空军公寓。在黑暗中很难看清任何东西，但那个身影看起来十几岁，身高约170厘米。直到第二天仔细检查时，博尔什一家才意识到晾衣绳上丢失了几件物品。

20
00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:35.000
were missing from their washing line. A pair of blue panties, elastic step-ins, and a silk half-slip skirt. The undergarments that Deirdre Kennedy had been dressed in. Police showed Cecil Carroll a photographic line-up of potential suspects, but he ruled each of them out as the prowler. Another resident of the household, 12-year-old Paul Borscht, had been at a barbecue with friends earlier that evening. He told police that when he returned home, he saw a young man walking in the direction
一条蓝色内裤、弹性紧身裤和一条丝绸半衬裙。正是迪尔德丽·肯尼迪所穿的内衣。警方给塞西尔·卡罗尔看了潜在嫌疑人的照片排查，但他排除了所有这些人作为潜行者的可能性。该住户的另一位成员，12岁的保罗·博尔什，那天晚上早些时候和朋友们参加了烧烤。他告诉警方，当他回家时，他看到一个年轻人正朝着石灰岩公园的方向走去。

21
00:13:35.000 --> 00:14:13.000
of Limestone Park. He was carrying something white over his shoulder. Police ultimately ruled Paul's sighting out, but they had no doubt that the man Cecil spied outside his window was the same person who killed Deirdre. News of Deirdre's death rattled the community. People not only felt deeply for the Kennedy family, but also feared for the safety of their own children. It was in everyone's best interest that the case be solved fast, and the public came forward
他的肩膀上扛着白色的东西。警方最终排除了保罗的目击证词，但他们毫不怀疑塞西尔在窗外窥视到的那个人就是杀死迪尔德丽的凶手。迪尔德丽去世的消息震惊了社区。人们不仅对肯尼迪一家深感同情，也为自己孩子的安全感到担忧。尽快破案符合每个人的最大利益，公众纷纷提供他们认为有帮助的任何细节。

22
00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:49.000
with any details they thought could help. Investigators considered whether the killer could have assaulted Deirdre at another location or inside a vehicle before dumping her body in Limestone Park. Witnesses reported seeing four different vehicles in the area on the night in question, but nothing pointed towards a clear suspect. Police urged the public to report anyone who was acting out of character in the days following the crime. They considered the possibility that more than one person could have been involved, but deemed
调查人员考虑了凶手是否可能在另一个地点或车内袭击了迪尔德丽，然后再将她的尸体丢弃在石灰岩公园。目击者报告说在案发当晚在该地区看到了四辆不同的车辆，但没有任何线索指向明确的嫌疑人。警方敦促公众举报在犯罪发生后的几天里行为反常的任何人。他们考虑了可能不止一人参与的可能性，但认为

23
00:14:49.000 --> 00:15:32.000
it much more likely that the perpetrator had acted alone. Extensive door knocks were carried out in a bid to determine whether any young males were absent from their homes on the night of Friday, April 13. Over three and a half thousand local males voluntarily provided their fingerprints to eliminate themselves from the investigation. And sex offenders and psychiatric patients were checked and ruled out. Several leads emerged, but none that led to any breakthroughs. Police deduced the killer either lived locally or was very familiar with the area.
凶手单独作案的可能性要大得多。警方进行了大规模的敲门调查，试图确定是否有年轻男性在4月13日星期五晚上不在家。超过三千五百名当地男性自愿提供了指纹以排除嫌疑。性犯罪者和精神病患者也经过了检查并被排除。出现了一些线索，但没有一条导致任何突破。警方推断凶手要么住在当地，要么非常熟悉该地区。

24
